    <body period="#tg_enact">
      <section eId="sec_1">
        <num>1</num>
        <heading>Short title and commencement</heading>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content><p>This Act may be cited as the Personal Data (Amendment) Act 2021.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content><p>Section 2 comes into force on 1 January 2022.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_3">
          <num>(3)</num>
          <content><p>Section 3 comes into force on a day appointed by the Minister by notice in the Gazette.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_4">
          <num>(4)</num>
          <content><p>Section 4 comes into force on 1 March 2023.</p></content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_2" period="#tg_s2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Retention period</heading>
        <content>
          <p>In <ref href="/akn/xa/act/2015/12/~sec_12__subsec_1" ulis:relation="amends">section 12(1) of the Personal Data Act 2015</ref>, for "seven years" substitute "five years".</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_3" ulis:status="prospective">
        <num>3</num>
        <heading>Backup copies</heading>
        <content>
          <p>After <ref href="/akn/xa/act/2015/12/~sec_12" ulis:relation="inserts">section 12 of the Personal Data Act 2015</ref> insert the following section: "12A Backup copies (1) For the purposes of section 12, personal data held in a backup copy is retained by the controller. (2) A controller may keep a backup copy for up to ninety days after the period in section 12(1) expires, if the backup copy is isolated from ordinary processing."</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_4" period="#tg_s4">
        <num>4</num>
        <heading>Repeal of transitional provision</heading>
        <content>
          <p><ref href="/akn/xa/act/2015/12/~sec_20" ulis:relation="repeals">Section 20 of the Personal Data Act 2015</ref> is repealed.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
    </body>
